Origin of the source files
--------------------------

Ported from Symphonia (symphonia-bundle-mp3 0.5.5, https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia),
Copyright (c) 2019-2022 The Project Symphonia Developers. These files keep their original
MPL-2.0 headers and were modified for LingOS (no_std + alloc, libm maths, crate-local bit
reader / Huffman codebooks / lazy tables / output buffer, boxed state for small kernel stacks,
panics on corrupt input turned into errors; changes noted in the file headers):

  src/common.rs
  src/header.rs
  src/layer1.rs            (src/layer1/mod.rs; also fixes mono streams reading two
                            allocations per sub-band)
  src/layer2.rs            (src/layer2/mod.rs)
  src/layer12.rs
  src/synthesis.rs
  src/layer3/mod.rs
  src/layer3/bitstream.rs
  src/layer3/codebooks.rs
  src/layer3/common.rs
  src/layer3/hybrid_synthesis.rs
  src/layer3/requantize.rs
  src/layer3/stereo.rs

Written for LingOS (also MPL-2.0, as part of this crate):

  src/lib.rs               (byte-stream front end: frame sync, ID3v2 skip, Xing / Info /
                            VBRI / LAME handling, partial-frame carry, decode_file)
  src/bits.rs              (errors, bit reader, Huffman codebook, Lazy static)
  src/tests.rs, examples/mpa_decode.rs
  tests/data/*             (short test clips encoded with ffmpeg / libmp3lame, and ffmpeg's
                            decodes of them as s16le references)
